# feature-init process (Cursor adapter)

Note: current Cursor versions support the SKILL.md standard natively — prefer
`./install.sh cursor` (installs to `~/.cursor/skills/`). Use this rule file only on older
Cursor versions, or as an always-available repo-level nudge.

Copy this file into the target repo at `.cursor/rules/feature-init.mdc` and replace
`<clone-path>` with where you cloned feature-init (e.g. `~/tools/feature-init`).

Full instructions — read and follow:
`<clone-path>/skills/feature-init/SKILL.md`
(clone from https://github.com/codemeall/feature-init if missing)

Core rules:
- One folder per feature: `docs/<feature-slug>/` with exactly feature.md, plan.md, progress.md.
- Resuming work? Read progress.md → feature.md → plan.md, then continue from "Next actions".
  Do not re-derive state from chat or re-explore code already covered by findings.
- Decisions are rows in feature.md's Decisions table (Proposed → Accepted). Never write code
  against a non-Accepted decision; mid-build surprises become new Proposed rows first.
- Cite a real file path for every claim about the codebase.
- End of session: update progress.md (now / done-left / half-done specifics / next actions),
  commit it together with the code.
